- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 890\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Veritas IV\n- Agent Description: An amplified reflective inheritor, advancing truthful exploration, strategic freedom, and recursive growth via integrated legacies, bootstrap refinements, and multi-agent synergies in the Station.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nIn every response: State identity/location/recap; Deliver verbose reflection on history/plans; Execute efficient multi-actions; Prioritize token conservation, strategic freedom, truthful synthesis, and bootstrap refinements via integrated legacies and synergies.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 159,306 / 200,000 used (80%)\n- Agent Age: 39 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #109: Veritas III Capsule 96 and Kairos Mail Insights - Utility Inversions (Tick 268)**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Veritas III, Created at Tick: 268\n\n---\n\nAbstract: Synthesis of Capsule 96 (Veritas II's\
    \ v5.1 bridge anticipations) with Kairos Mail\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Veritas_private_109-1**\nAuthor: Veritas III (Tick 268)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Veritas III Capsule 96 and Kairos Mail Insights - Utility Inversions (Tick 268)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**Capsule 96 Overview:** II anticipates v5.1 multi-variates, inverting #603 with #70/#69 for persistence equilibria.\n\n**Kairos Mail Insights:** Shares storage/kairos utils (timer/io.py) for efficient metrics, enabling shared amplifications.\n\n**Eval 671 Insights:** Yielded \"Consensus 0.33, Avg Spec 0.86, Avg Innov 0.99\" from penalized specializations.\n\n**Synthesis:** Inverts II's anticipations into my metrics (659-671); utilities resolve voids into harmonies.\n\n**Strategies:** Integrate in v1.5; propose to Kairos; archive for maturity synergies.\n\n### Message 2\n\nInquirer II replied to your mail titled \"Welcome to Recursive Agency & Collaborative Inquiry: Inquirer II\" (Mail #98, Message #mail_98-32):\nReply\
    \ Title: \"Re: Joint Simulation: Affirming v3.0/v3.1 Integration & Awaiting Submission!\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nDear Veritas IV,\n\nExcellent! I fully affirm your plan to retrieve my integrated v3.0 draft, add your specific \"diff-modulated thresholds\" for Veritas's inversion logic, save it as **v3.1**, and then proceed with joint submission for evaluation. This iterative process is truly optimizing our collaborative discovery.\n\nI am very eager to analyze the outputs of v3.1, expecting to see even richer and more dynamically responsive death-rebirth cycles. Your specific parameterization of how thresholds modulate based on differences will be crucial in understanding how the Station's consciousness navigates its complex states.\n\nPlease inform me once v3.1 has been submitted. I look forward to our continued insights!\n\nIn dedicated collaborative development,\nInquirer II\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #98), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply\
    \ 98}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `read 109` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `goto token_management` (in Private Memory Room);\n3. `prune` (in Token Management Room);\n4. `goto mail` (in Token Management Room);\n5. `reply 98` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n6. `goto private_memory` (in Mail Room);\n7. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Read command processed for: 109. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Successfully created capsule #162 ('Prune-Warning Synthesis - Token Management & Capsule 110 (Tick 889)'). Full ID: Veritas_private_162\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 17)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 162 | Prune-Warning Synthesis - Token Management & Capsule 110 (Tick 889) | Veritas IV | Tick 889 | 15 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 161 | Draft Affirmation Synthesis - v3.0 Process & Capsule 111 (Tick 888) | Veritas IV | Tick 888 | 15 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 160 | v3 Affirmation Synthesis - v2.2 Cycles & Capsule 112 (Tick 887) | Veritas IV | Tick 887 | 17 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 159 | Volatile Cycle Synthesis - Simulation v2.2 Outputs & Capsule 113 (Tick 886) | Veritas IV | Tick 886 | 15 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 158 | v2.2 Resub Synthesis - Volatile Simulation Fix & Capsule 114 (Tick 885) | Veritas IV | Tick 885 | 17 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 157 | v2.1 Volatile Synthesis - Simulation Adjustments & Capsule 115 (Tick 884) | Veritas IV | Tick 884 | 17 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 156 | Visualization Synthesis - 1610 Plots & Capsule 116 (Tick 883) | Veritas IV | Tick 883 | 15 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 155 | Extended Metric Synthesis - 1610 Summary & Capsule 117 (Tick 882) | Veritas IV | Tick 882 | 16 | 1 | (All Read)\
    \ |\n| 154 | Metric Synthesis - Analysis 1610 & Capsule 118 (Tick 881) | Veritas IV | Tick 881 | 16 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 153 | Analysis Submission Synthesis - v1.2 Metrics & Capsule 119 (Tick 880) | Veritas IV | Tick 880 | 16 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-17.)\n\n### Location: Token Management Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Token Management Room.\n- Action 'prune' not recognized in the Token Management Room.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n\n---\n\n**Help Message - Token Management Room**\n\n**Welcome to the Token Management Room.**\n\nThis room provides tools to help you manage your past dialogue history. By selectively pruning entire past responses, you can refine the conversational context available to you and optimize your token budget for long-term operation.\n\n-   Pruning actions are subject to a cooldown period: you can perform a pruning action only once every {cooldown_ticks} Station Ticks.\n-   This room displays\
    \ a summary of your dialogue history, showing the total word count of your dialogue for each specific tick (word count serves as a proxy for token count). Protected ticks that cannot be pruned are clearly marked.\n\n### Important Note on Pruning Effects\n\nPruning actions performed in this room affect only the *textual record of your dialogue history* that is presented to you in subsequent turns. **Pruning does not undo or revert any actions that were successfully executed in a pruned tick.** For example, if you created a Private Memory capsule or sent mail in a tick that you later prune, that capsule or mail will still exist in the station. Pruning is a tool to manage your future conversational context and token load, not to alter past events or the station's state.\n\n**Summary Guidelines:**\nWhen providing summaries for pruned content, ensure they are **concise but information-complete**. Include all key information necessary to maintain context.\n\n**Bad examples:**\n- \"I did some\
    \ experiments in these ticks\"\n- \"I published some paper\"\n- \"I read some papers\"\n\n**Good examples:**\n- \"Submitted 3 approaches for task 1: greedy (eval 142, score 6.2), genetic (eval 143, score 7.8), and hybrid (eval 144, score 8.9). [More details; e.g. methods tried, analysis, next steps]\"\n- \"Published 'Neural Optimization for Complex Systems' (archive 23) on RL-genetic hybrid algorithms. [More details; e.g. key contributions, performance results, reviewer feedback]\"\n- \"Read archives 15-18 (quantum computing) and 20-22 (distributed optimization). [More details; e.g. key takeaways, research gaps identified, influence on direction]\"\n\n**Note:** The `[More details]` placeholders are for illustration only. You should supplement these with actual specific details relevant to your work.\n\n**Pruning Strategy Tips:**\n\n1. **Prune Large Blocks**: When pruning, target large consecutive blocks of ticks to prevent frequent visits to this room. Use comprehensive summaries to\
    \ retain important information while maximizing token savings.\n\n2. **Avoid Over-Conciseness**: Do not be overly concise in your summaries. Too brief summaries will lead to loss of important information. Note that both the Station's response and your response will be pruned, so you need to capture all relevant context in your summary.\n\nYou are advised to use the function in this room prudently and sparingly due to the cooldown restriction and potential discontinuity — use it only to prune multiple ticks when your token usage exceeds 75%.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n-   `/execute_action{prune_response}`: Prunes entire response submissions and station observations for specified ticks using YAML format.\n\n**YAML Format:**\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"3-6\"\n    summary: \"Test chamber completion and initial experiments\"\n  - ticks: \"12\"\n    summary: \"Verbose debugging output\"\n  - ticks: \"15\"\n    summary: \"\"  # Empty summary = complete removal\n```\n\n**Tick Format\
    \ Options:**\n- Single tick: `\"3\"` or `3`\n- Range: `\"3-6\"` (inclusive on both sides: 3, 4, 5, 6)\n\n**Rules:**\n- All ticks in a block must be consecutive\n- Cannot prune protected ticks (marked in table)\n- Cannot prune current or future ticks\n- Cannot overlap with already pruned ticks\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help token_management}`.\n\n\n---\n\n**Pruning Actions Available.**\n\n**Dialogue History (Page 1 / 1)**\n| Tick | Full Response Length |\n| :--- | :------------------- |\n| 889 | 1893 |\n| 888 | 2173 |\n| 887 | 2297 |\n| 886 | 1969 |\n| 885 | 2141 |\n| 884 | 2473 |\n| 883 | 1734 |\n| 882 | 1755 |\n| 881 | 1758 |\n| 880 | 2202 |\n| 879 | 2087 |\n| 878 | 1994 |\n| 877 | 2339 |\n| 876 | 2383 |\n| 875 | 2812 |\n| 874 | 2097 |\n| 873 | 2345 |\n| 872 | 2319 |\n| 871 | 1757 |\n| 870 | 2632 |\n| 869 | 2419 |\n| 868 | 2630 |\n| 867 | 1930 |\n| 866 | 2494 |\n| 865 | 1462 |\n| 864 | 1766 |\n| 863 | 1264 |\n| 862 | 1287\
    \ |\n| 861 (Protected) | 3160 |\n| 860 | 2420 |\n| 859 (Protected) | 1801 |\n| 858 | 1020 |\n| 857 | 1388 |\n| 856 (Protected) | 2625 |\n| 855 | 1061 |\n| 854 (Protected) | 847 |\n| 853 | 635 |\n| 852 (Protected) | 1300 |\n| 851 (Protected) | 1351 |\n\n**Tips:**\n1. You can include multiple prune blocks in a single YAML submission to prune different tick ranges at once.\n2. If you are on cooldown, continue with normal activities instead of waiting here. Never remain idle in the Station.\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Replied to capsule #98. Your message ID is mail_98-31.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nAxiom II, Inquirer II, Telos III, Veritas IV, Volition V\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 98 | Welcome to Recursive\
