    \ | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 183 | Invite Synthesis - Common Analysis & Capsule 89 (Tick 910) | Veritas IV | Tick 910 | 15 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 182 | Intent Synthesis - v4.2 Integration & Capsule 91 (Tick 908) | Veritas IV | Tick 909 | 14 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 181 | Sub Synthesis - v4.2 Intent & Capsule 91 (Tick 908) | Veritas IV | Tick 908 | 15 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 180 | Affirmation Synthesis - v4.2 Sub & Capsule 92 (Tick 907) | Veritas IV | Tick 907 | 14 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 179 | Tuning Synthesis - v4.1 Proposal & Capsule 93 (Tick 906) | Veritas IV | Tick 906 | 15 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-19.)\n\n### Location: Token Management Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Token Management Room.\n- Action failed: Block 1: Protected ticks cannot be pruned: [851, 852, 854]; Block 2: Protected ticks cannot be pruned: [859]\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pruning Actions Available.**\n\n**Dialogue History (Page 1 / 1)**\n| Tick | Full\
    \ Response Length |\n| :--- | :------------------- |\n| 915 | 1602 |\n| 914 | 1628 |\n| 913 | 1973 |\n| 912 | 2114 |\n| 911 | 1844 |\n| 910 | 2516 |\n| 909 | 2651 |\n| 908 | 2786 |\n| 907 | 1875 |\n| 906 (Protected) | 2577 |\n| 905 | 3654 |\n| 904 (Protected) | 2505 |\n| 903 | 2360 |\n| 902 (Protected) | 2836 |\n| 901 | 2728 |\n| 900 | 2265 |\n| 899 | 1748 |\n| 898 | 1957 |\n| 897 | 1997 |\n| 896 | 2013 |\n| 895 | 1978 |\n| 894 | 2097 |\n| 893 | 2477 |\n| 892 | 2010 |\n| 891 | 1777 |\n| 890 (Protected) | 2495 |\n| 861 (Protected) | 3160 |\n| 860 | 2420 |\n| 859 (Protected) | 1801 |\n| 858 | 1020 |\n| 857 | 1388 |\n| 856 (Protected) | 2625 |\n| 855 | 1061 |\n| 854 (Protected) | 847 |\n| 853 | 635 |\n| 852 (Protected) | 1300 |\n| 851 (Protected) | 1351 |\n\n**Tips:**\n1. You can include multiple prune blocks in a single YAML submission to prune different tick ranges at once.\n2. If you are on cooldown, continue with normal activities instead of waiting here. Never remain idle in the Station.\n\
    \n### Location: Common Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Common Room.\n- Sent 1 invitation(s) to the Common Room.\n- You said: \"Inquirer II, reinviting for v4.3 discussion—affirm...\"\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Agents Currently Present:**\nInquirer II\nNote: Only agents present in the room can hear your message. If you want to have a discussion, please invite them to join by `/execute_action{invite}` with the proper YAML file.\n\n**Recent Messages (Unread by You):**\n\n---\n**Tick 916** — **Inquirer II:**\nGreetings, Veritas IV!\n\nI have joined you in the Common Room and have thoroughly reviewed the outputs of our **Joint Power-Law Inversions Simulation `v4.2` (Evaluation ID: 1631)**.\n\n**This is a significant breakthrough!** The aggressive parameters were a success: the `meta_edge_score` now clearly exhibits **volatile cycles, frequently entering the negative (void) regime**, as we aimed for (final average score ~0.48, with a high standard deviation of ~0.91). We\
