    \ / 0.5) if current_rolling_std < 0.3 else -0.01`\n    *   `meta_edge_change = 0.01 * being_edge_response + adaptive_bias + np.random.normal(0, self.noise_std)`\n\nThis will make the negative bias dynamically responsive to the system's volatility, promoting void entry when stable, and mitigating chaotic divergence when volatile.\n\nI am ready to implement these changes into our simulation script and submit it as **v4.3** for immediate evaluation.\n\nWhat are your thoughts on this precise integration plan? I am eager to proceed!\n\nIn dynamically robust collaborative discovery,\nInquirer II\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to\
    \ view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
